{"parentUuid":"cf164cec-5a99-4a01-8e88-1aea3c1673ba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LXKCdFvKARubNp6GnAhmGd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017nDqCmFNkdK1p5yqiTDykx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/goose-guest/Documents/work/cli/CONTRIBUTING.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_read_input_tokens":31526,"output_tokens":93,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":261,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":93,"cache_read_input_tokens":31526,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":261},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Caxz1sDptHT1px7CZ1agp","type":"assistant","uuid":"53816909-cbed-4ca1-89db-8e6a4d73267c","timestamp":"2026-05-12T16:23:31.267Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/goose-guest/Documents/work/external-agents/.claude/worktrees/nervous-lovelace-2f4b1f","sessionId":"5ec529ca-57a1-47f3-a7d2-fb63984f64a9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"claude/nervous-lovelace-2f4b1f"}
{"parentUuid":"53816909-cbed-4ca1-89db-8e6a4d73267c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e783faea-ac5e-45f6-891b-11cf8b9f3d2a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nDqCmFNkdK1p5yqiTDykx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Contributing to the Entire CLI\n2\t\n3\tThank you for your interest in contributing to Entire! We welcome contributions from everyone.\n4\t\n5\tPlease read our [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) before participating.\n6\t\n7\t> **New to Entire?** See the [First-Time Contributors guide](docs/first-time-contributors.md) for a step-by-step first contribution walkthrough, or the [README](README.md) for setup and usage documentation.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Before You Code: Discuss First\n12\t\n13\tThe fastest way to get a contribution merged is to align with maintainers before writing code. Please **open an issue first** using our [issue templates](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/new/choose) and wait for maintainer feedback before starting implementation.\n14\t\n15\t### Contribution Workflow\n16\t\n17\t1. **Open an issue** describing the problem or feature\n18\t2. **Wait for maintainer feedback** -- we may have relevant context or plans\n19\t3. **Get approval** before starting implementation\n20\t4. **Submit your PR** referencing the approved issue\n21\t5. **Address all feedback** including automated Copilot comments\n22\t6. **Maintainer review and merge**\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## First-Time Contributors\n27\t\n28\tNew to the project? Welcome! Start with the\n29\t[First-Time Contributors guide](docs/first-time-contributors.md). It explains\n30\thow to find a comfortable issue, ask for a scoped starter task, set up the repo,\n31\tuse AI responsibly, run the right checks, and open your first pull request.\n32\t\n33\t### Starter Contributions\n34\t\n35\tWe recommend starting with:\n36\t\n37\t- **A bug you can reproduce** - Add the missing test and a narrow fix\n38\t- **CLI output improvements** - Clarify confusing messages or help text\n39\t- **Test contributions** - Cover existing behavior with a focused test\n40\t- **Setup friction** - Improve README or contributor instructions after you hit a real problem\n41\t\n42\tBrowse [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues), or ask in the\n43\t`#looking-for-contributors` Discord channel if you want help finding a\n44\tstarter-sized slice.\n45\t\n46\tUsing a coding agent while contributing is welcome, but you are responsible for\n47\tthe final diff. Review AI-generated changes yourself before opening a PR.\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## Submitting Issues\n52\t\n53\tAll feature requests, bug reports, and general issues should be submitted through [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues). Please search for existing issues before opening a new one.\n54\t\n55\tFor security-related issues, see the Security section below.\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## Security\n60\t\n61\tIf you discover a security vulnerability, **do not report it through GitHub Issues**. Instead, please follow the instructions in our [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) file for responsible disclosure. All security reports are kept confidential as described in SECURITY.md.\n62\t\n63\t---\n64\t\n65\t## Contributions & Communication\n66\t\n67\tContributions and communications are expected to occur through:\n68\t\n69\t- [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) - Bug reports and feature requests\n70\t- [Discord](https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S) - Questions, general conversation, and real-time support\n71\t\n72\tPlease represent the project and community respectfully in all public and private interactions.\n73\t\n74\t\n75\t## How to Contribute\n76\t\n77\t\n78\tThere are many ways to contribute:\n79\t\n80\t- **Feature requests** - Open a [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) to discuss your idea\n81\t- **Bug reports** - Report issues via [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) (see [Reporting Bugs](#reporting-bugs))\n82\t- **Code contributions** - Fix bugs, add features, improve tests\n83\t- **Documentation** - Improve guides, fix typos, add examples\n84\t- **Community** - Help others, answer questions, share knowledge\n85\t\n86\t\n87\t## Reporting Bugs\n88\t\n89\tGood bug reports help us fix issues quickly. When reporting a bug, please include:\n90\t\n91\t### Required Information\n92\t\n93\t1. **Entire CLI version** - run `entire version`\n94\t2. **Operating system**\n95\t3. **Go version** - run `go version`\n96\t\n97\t### What to Include\n98\t\n99\tPlease answer these questions in your bug report:\n100\t\n101\t1. **What did you do?** - Include the exact commands you ran\n102\t2. **What did you expect to happen?**\n103\t3. **What actually happened?** - Include the full error message or unexpected output\n104\t4. **Can you reproduce it?** - Does it happen every time or intermittently?\n105\t5. **Any additional context?** - Logs, screenshots, or related issues\n106\t\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t## Local Setup\n110\t\n111\t### Prerequisites\n112\t\n113\t- **Go 1.26.x** - Check with `go version`\n114\t- **mise** - Task runner and version manager. Install with `curl https://mise.run | sh`\n115\t\n116\t### Clone and Install\n117\t\n118\t```bash\n119\t# Clone the repository\n120\tgit clone https://github.com/entireio/cli.git\n121\tcd cli\n122\t\n123\t# Trust the mise configuration (required on first setup)\n124\tmise trust\n125\t\n126\t# Install dependencies (mise will install the correct Go version)\n127\tmise install\n128\t\n129\t# Download Go modules\n130\tgo mod download\n131\t\n132\t# Build the CLI\n133\tmise run build\n134\t\n135\t# Verify setup by running tests\n136\tmise run test\n137\t```\n138\t\n139\t> See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for detailed architecture and development reference.\n140\t\n141\t---\n142\t\n143\t## Making Changes\n144\t\n145\t1. **Create a branch** for your changes:\n146\t   ```bash\n147\t   git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n148\t   ```\n149\t\n150\t2. **Make your changes** - follow the [Code Style](#code-style) guidelines\n151\t\n152\t3. **Test your changes** - see [Testing](#testing)\n153\t\n154\t4. **Commit** with clear, descriptive messages:\n155\t   ```bash\n156\t   git commit -m \"Add feature: description of what you added\"\n157\t   ```\n158\t\n159\t---\n160\t\n161\t## Code Style\n162\t\n163\tFollow standard Go idioms and conventions. For detailed guidance, see the **Go Code Style** section in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n164\t\n165\t### Key Points\n166\t\n167\t- **Error handling**: Handle all errors explicitly - don't leave them unchecked\n168\t- **Formatting**: Code must pass `gofmt` (run `mise run fmt`)\n169\t- **Linting**: Code must pass `golangci-lint` (run `mise run lint`)\n170\t- **Naming**: Use meaningful, descriptive names following Go conventions\n171\t\n172\t---\n173\t\n174\t## Testing\n175\t\n176\t> See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for complete testing documentation.\n177\t\n178\t```bash\n179\t# Unit tests - always run before committing\n180\tmise run test\n181\t\n182\t# Integration tests\n183\tmise run test:integration\n184\t\n185\t# Full CI suite\n186\tmise run test:ci\n187\t```\n188\t\n189\tIntegration tests use the `//go:build integration` build tag and are located in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`.\n190\t\n191\t---\n192\t\n193\t## Creating an Agent\n194\t\n195\t\n196\tEntire supports two ways to create agents:\n197\t\n198\t### 1. Claude Code Agent Personas (Markdown)\n199\t\n200\tThese are markdown files that define specialized behaviors for Claude Code (e.g., developer, reviewer, etc.).\n201\t\n202\t- **Location:** `.claude/agents/`\n203\t- **Structure:**\n204\t   ```markdown\n205\t   ---\n206\t   name: my-agent\n207\t   description: What this agent does\n208\t   model: opus\n209\t   color: blue\n210\t   ---\n211\t\n212\t   # Agent Name\n213\t   You are a **[Role]** with expertise in [domain].\n214\t\n215\t   ## Core Principles\n216\t   - Principle 1\n217\t   - Principle 2\n218\t\n219\t   ## Process\n220\t   1. Step 1\n221\t   2. Step 2\n222\t\n223\t   ## Output Format\n224\t   How to structure responses...\n225\t   ```\n226\t- **To invoke:** Create a matching command in `.claude/commands/` that spawns the agent via the Task tool.\n227\t- **Examples:**\n228\t   - `.claude/agents/dev.md` - TDD Developer\n229\t   - `.claude/agents/reviewer.md` - Code Reviewer\n230\t\n231\t### 2. Coding Agent Integrations (Go)\n232\t\n233\tThese are Go implementations that integrate Entire with different AI coding tools (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, etc.) using the Agent abstraction layer.\n234\t\n235\t- **Location:** `cmd/entire/cli/agent/`\n236\t- **Steps:**\n237\t   1. Implement the `Agent` interface in `agent/agent.go`\n238\t   2. Register your agent in the agent registry\n239\t   3. Add setup and hook configuration as needed\n240\t   4. Ensure session and checkpoint tracking is handled per the abstraction\n241\t- **Reference:** See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for architecture and code examples.\n242\t\n243\t---\n244\t\n245\t**Which should I use?**\n246\t\n247\t- Use a persona markdown agent if you want to create a new role or workflow for Claude Code.\n248\t- Use a coding agent integration if you want to add support for a new AI coding tool or extend agent capabilities in the CLI.\n249\t\n250\t---\n251\t\n252\t## Submitting a Pull Request\n253\t\n254\t### Before You Submit\n255\t\n256\t- **Related issue exists and is approved** -- Your PR references an issue where a maintainer has acknowledged the approach. (Exceptions: typo corrections, wording-only updates, and maintainer-scoped starter tasks.)\n257\t- **Linting passes** -- Run `mise run lint` (includes golangci-lint, gofmt, gomod, shellcheck)\n258\t- **Tests pass** -- Run `mise run test` to verify your changes\n259\t- **Tests included** -- New Go code and functionality should have accompanying tests\n260\t- **Entire checkpoint trailers included** -- See [Using Entire While Contributing](#using-entire-while-contributing) below\n261\t\n262\tPRs that skip these steps are likely to be closed without merge.\n263\t\n264\t### Submitting\n265\t\n266\t1. **Push** your branch to your fork\n267\t2. **Open a PR** against the `main` branch\n268\t3. **Describe your changes** -- Link the related issue, summarize what changed and what testing you did\n269\t4. **Address Copilot feedback** -- See [Responding to Automated Review](#responding-to-automated-review)\n270\t5. **Wait for maintainer review**\n271\t\n272\t---\n273\t\n274\t## Responding to Automated Review\n275\t\n276\tCo-pilot agent reviews every PR and provides feedback on code quality, potential bugs, and project conventions.\n277\t\n278\t**Read and respond to every Copilot comment.** PRs with unaddressed Copilot feedback will not move to maintainer review.\n279\t\n280\t- **Fixed** -- Push a commit addressing the issue.\n281\t- **Disagree** -- Reply explaining your reasoning. The Copilot isn't always right.\n282\t- **Question** -- Ask for clarification. We're happy to help.\n283\t\n284\tAddressing Copilot feedback upfront is the fastest path to maintainer review.\n285\t\n286\t---\n287\t\n288\t## Using Entire While Contributing\n289\t\n290\tWe use Entire on Entire. When contributing, install the Entire CLI and let it capture your coding sessions -- this gives us valuable dogfooding data and helps improve the tool.\n291\t\n292\t### Setup\n293\t\n294\tInstall the latest version of the Entire CLI (see [installation docs](https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation)) and verify with `entire version`. Entire is already configured in this repository, so there's no need to run `entire enable`.\n295\t\n296\t### Checkpoint Trailers\n297\t\n298\tAll commits should include `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers from your sessions. These are added automatically by the `prepare-commit-msg` hook when Entire is enabled. The trailers link your commits to session metadata on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch.\n299\t\n300\t### Sessions Branch\n301\t\n302\tWhen you push your PR branch, Entire can automatically push the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch alongside it (if `push_sessions` is enabled in your settings). Include this in your PR so maintainers can review the session context behind your changes.\n303\t\n304\t---\n305\t\n306\t## Troubleshooting\n307\t\n308\t### Common Setup Issues\n309\t\n310\t**`go mod download` fails with timeout**\n311\t```bash\n312\t# Try using direct mode\n313\tGOPROXY=direct go mod download\n314\t```\n315\t\n316\t**`mise install` fails**\n317\t```bash\n318\t# Ensure mise is properly installed\n319\tcurl https://mise.run | sh\n320\t\n321\t# Reload your shell\n322\tsource ~/.zshrc  # or ~/.bashrc\n323\t```\n324\t\n325\t**Binary not updating after rebuild**\n326\t```bash\n327\t# Check which binary is being used\n328\twhich entire\n329\ttype -a entire\n330\t\n331\t# You may have multiple installations - update the correct path\n332\t```\n333\t\n334\t---\n335\t\n336\t## Community\n337\t\n338\tJoin the Entire community:\n339\t\n340\t- **Discord** - [Join our server][discord] for discussions and support\n341\t\n342\t[discord]: https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S\n343\t\n344\t---\n345\t\n346\t## Additional Resources\n347\t\n348\t- [README](README.md) - Setup and usage documentation\n349\t- [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) - Architecture and development reference (Claude Code)\n350\t- [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) - Architecture and development reference (Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI)\n351\t- [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) - Community guidelines\n352\t- [Security Policy](SECURITY.md) - Reporting security vulnerabilities\n353\t\n354\t---\n355\t\n356\tThank you for contributing!\n357\t"}]},"uuid":"1f52eb11-1f65-4b23-b977-ff227d86403f","timestamp":"2026-05-12T16:23:31.284Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/goose-guest/Documents/work/cli/CONTRIBUTING.md","content":"# Contributing to the Entire CLI\n\nThank you for your interest in contributing to Entire! We welcome contributions from everyone.\n\nPlease read our [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) before participating.\n\n> **New to Entire?** See the [First-Time Contributors guide](docs/first-time-contributors.md) for a step-by-step first contribution walkthrough, or the [README](README.md) for setup and usage documentation.\n\n---\n\n## Before You Code: Discuss First\n\nThe fastest way to get a contribution merged is to align with maintainers before writing code. Please **open an issue first** using our [issue templates](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/new/choose) and wait for maintainer feedback before starting implementation.\n\n### Contribution Workflow\n\n1. **Open an issue** describing the problem or feature\n2. **Wait for maintainer feedback** -- we may have relevant context or plans\n3. **Get approval** before starting implementation\n4. **Submit your PR** referencing the approved issue\n5. **Address all feedback** including automated Copilot comments\n6. **Maintainer review and merge**\n\n---\n\n## First-Time Contributors\n\nNew to the project? Welcome! Start with the\n[First-Time Contributors guide](docs/first-time-contributors.md). It explains\nhow to find a comfortable issue, ask for a scoped starter task, set up the repo,\nuse AI responsibly, run the right checks, and open your first pull request.\n\n### Starter Contributions\n\nWe recommend starting with:\n\n- **A bug you can reproduce** - Add the missing test and a narrow fix\n- **CLI output improvements** - Clarify confusing messages or help text\n- **Test contributions** - Cover existing behavior with a focused test\n- **Setup friction** - Improve README or contributor instructions after you hit a real problem\n\nBrowse [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues), or ask in the\n`#looking-for-contributors` Discord channel if you want help finding a\nstarter-sized slice.\n\nUsing a coding agent while contributing is welcome, but you are responsible for\nthe final diff. Review AI-generated changes yourself before opening a PR.\n\n---\n\n## Submitting Issues\n\nAll feature requests, bug reports, and general issues should be submitted through [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues). Please search for existing issues before opening a new one.\n\nFor security-related issues, see the Security section below.\n\n---\n\n## Security\n\nIf you discover a security vulnerability, **do not report it through GitHub Issues**. Instead, please follow the instructions in our [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) file for responsible disclosure. All security reports are kept confidential as described in SECURITY.md.\n\n---\n\n## Contributions & Communication\n\nContributions and communications are expected to occur through:\n\n- [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) - Bug reports and feature requests\n- [Discord](https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S) - Questions, general conversation, and real-time support\n\nPlease represent the project and community respectfully in all public and private interactions.\n\n\n## How to Contribute\n\n\nThere are many ways to contribute:\n\n- **Feature requests** - Open a [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) to discuss your idea\n- **Bug reports** - Report issues via [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) (see [Reporting Bugs](#reporting-bugs))\n- **Code contributions** - Fix bugs, add features, improve tests\n- **Documentation** - Improve guides, fix typos, add examples\n- **Community** - Help others, answer questions, share knowledge\n\n\n## Reporting Bugs\n\nGood bug reports help us fix issues quickly. When reporting a bug, please include:\n\n### Required Information\n\n1. **Entire CLI version** - run `entire version`\n2. **Operating system**\n3. **Go version** - run `go version`\n\n### What to Include\n\nPlease answer these questions in your bug report:\n\n1. **What did you do?** - Include the exact commands you ran\n2. **What did you expect to happen?**\n3. **What actually happened?** - Include the full error message or unexpected output\n4. **Can you reproduce it?** - Does it happen every time or intermittently?\n5. **Any additional context?** - Logs, screenshots, or related issues\n\n---\n\n## Local Setup\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- **Go 1.26.x** - Check with `go version`\n- **mise** - Task runner and version manager. Install with `curl https://mise.run | sh`\n\n### Clone and Install\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/entireio/cli.git\ncd cli\n\n# Trust the mise configuration (required on first setup)\nmise trust\n\n# Install dependencies (mise will install the correct Go version)\nmise install\n\n# Download Go modules\ngo mod download\n\n# Build the CLI\nmise run build\n\n# Verify setup by running tests\nmise run test\n```\n\n> See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for detailed architecture and development reference.\n\n---\n\n## Making Changes\n\n1. **Create a branch** for your changes:\n   ```bash\n   git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n   ```\n\n2. **Make your changes** - follow the [Code Style](#code-style) guidelines\n\n3. **Test your changes** - see [Testing](#testing)\n\n4. **Commit** with clear, descriptive messages:\n   ```bash\n   git commit -m \"Add feature: description of what you added\"\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## Code Style\n\nFollow standard Go idioms and conventions. For detailed guidance, see the **Go Code Style** section in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n\n### Key Points\n\n- **Error handling**: Handle all errors explicitly - don't leave them unchecked\n- **Formatting**: Code must pass `gofmt` (run `mise run fmt`)\n- **Linting**: Code must pass `golangci-lint` (run `mise run lint`)\n- **Naming**: Use meaningful, descriptive names following Go conventions\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\n> See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for complete testing documentation.\n\n```bash\n# Unit tests - always run before committing\nmise run test\n\n# Integration tests\nmise run test:integration\n\n# Full CI suite\nmise run test:ci\n```\n\nIntegration tests use the `//go:build integration` build tag and are located in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`.\n\n---\n\n## Creating an Agent\n\n\nEntire supports two ways to create agents:\n\n### 1. Claude Code Agent Personas (Markdown)\n\nThese are markdown files that define specialized behaviors for Claude Code (e.g., developer, reviewer, etc.).\n\n- **Location:** `.claude/agents/`\n- **Structure:**\n   ```markdown\n   ---\n   name: my-agent\n   description: What this agent does\n   model: opus\n   color: blue\n   ---\n\n   # Agent Name\n   You are a **[Role]** with expertise in [domain].\n\n   ## Core Principles\n   - Principle 1\n   - Principle 2\n\n   ## Process\n   1. Step 1\n   2. Step 2\n\n   ## Output Format\n   How to structure responses...\n   ```\n- **To invoke:** Create a matching command in `.claude/commands/` that spawns the agent via the Task tool.\n- **Examples:**\n   - `.claude/agents/dev.md` - TDD Developer\n   - `.claude/agents/reviewer.md` - Code Reviewer\n\n### 2. Coding Agent Integrations (Go)\n\nThese are Go implementations that integrate Entire with different AI coding tools (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, etc.) using the Agent abstraction layer.\n\n- **Location:** `cmd/entire/cli/agent/`\n- **Steps:**\n   1. Implement the `Agent` interface in `agent/agent.go`\n   2. Register your agent in the agent registry\n   3. Add setup and hook configuration as needed\n   4. Ensure session and checkpoint tracking is handled per the abstraction\n- **Reference:** See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for architecture and code examples.\n\n---\n\n**Which should I use?**\n\n- Use a persona markdown agent if you want to create a new role or workflow for Claude Code.\n- Use a coding agent integration if you want to add support for a new AI coding tool or extend agent capabilities in the CLI.\n\n---\n\n## Submitting a Pull Request\n\n### Before You Submit\n\n- **Related issue exists and is approved** -- Your PR references an issue where a maintainer has acknowledged the approach. (Exceptions: typo corrections, wording-only updates, and maintainer-scoped starter tasks.)\n- **Linting passes** -- Run `mise run lint` (includes golangci-lint, gofmt, gomod, shellcheck)\n- **Tests pass** -- Run `mise run test` to verify your changes\n- **Tests included** -- New Go code and functionality should have accompanying tests\n- **Entire checkpoint trailers included** -- See [Using Entire While Contributing](#using-entire-while-contributing) below\n\nPRs that skip these steps are likely to be closed without merge.\n\n### Submitting\n\n1. **Push** your branch to your fork\n2. **Open a PR** against the `main` branch\n3. **Describe your changes** -- Link the related issue, summarize what changed and what testing you did\n4. **Address Copilot feedback** -- See [Responding to Automated Review](#responding-to-automated-review)\n5. **Wait for maintainer review**\n\n---\n\n## Responding to Automated Review\n\nCo-pilot agent reviews every PR and provides feedback on code quality, potential bugs, and project conventions.\n\n**Read and respond to every Copilot comment.** PRs with unaddressed Copilot feedback will not move to maintainer review.\n\n- **Fixed** -- Push a commit addressing the issue.\n- **Disagree** -- Reply explaining your reasoning. The Copilot isn't always right.\n- **Question** -- Ask for clarification. We're happy to help.\n\nAddressing Copilot feedback upfront is the fastest path to maintainer review.\n\n---\n\n## Using Entire While Contributing\n\nWe use Entire on Entire. When contributing, install the Entire CLI and let it capture your coding sessions -- this gives us valuable dogfooding data and helps improve the tool.\n\n### Setup\n\nInstall the latest version of the Entire CLI (see [installation docs](https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation)) and verify with `entire version`. Entire is already configured in this repository, so there's no need to run `entire enable`.\n\n### Checkpoint Trailers\n\nAll commits should include `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers from your sessions. These are added automatically by the `prepare-commit-msg` hook when Entire is enabled. The trailers link your commits to session metadata on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch.\n\n### Sessions Branch\n\nWhen you push your PR branch, Entire can automatically push the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch alongside it (if `push_sessions` is enabled in your settings). Include this in your PR so maintainers can review the session context behind your changes.\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Setup Issues\n\n**`go mod download` fails with timeout**\n```bash\n# Try using direct mode\nGOPROXY=direct go mod download\n```\n\n**`mise install` fails**\n```bash\n# Ensure mise is properly installed\ncurl https://mise.run | sh\n\n# Reload your shell\nsource ~/.zshrc  # or ~/.bashrc\n```\n\n**Binary not updating after rebuild**\n```bash\n# Check which binary is being used\nwhich entire\ntype -a entire\n\n# You may have multiple installations - update the correct path\n```\n\n---\n\n## Community\n\nJoin the Entire community:\n\n- **Discord** - [Join our server][discord] for discussions and support\n\n[discord]: https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S\n\n---\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- [README](README.md) - Setup and usage documentation\n- [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) - Architecture and development reference (Claude Code)\n- [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) - Architecture and development reference (Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI)\n- [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) - Community guidelines\n- [Security Policy](SECURITY.md) - Reporting security vulnerabilities\n\n---\n\nThank you for contributing!\n","numLines":357,"startLine":1,"totalLines":357}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"53816909-cbed-4ca1-89db-8e6a4d73267c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/goose-guest/Documents/work/external-agents/.claude/worktrees/nervous-lovelace-2f4b