{"parentUuid":"3ed4347e-3e8c-4fa3-85c0-cf6618797fd4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/goose-guest/Documents/work/external-agents/.claude/worktrees/nervous-lovelace-2f4b1f/CONTRIBUTING.md","snippet":"1\t# Contributing to Entire External Agents\n2\t\n3\tThank you for your interest in contributing! This repository hosts the standalone\n4\texternal agent binaries (`entire-agent-<name>`) that extend the\n5\t[Entire CLI](https://github.com/entireio/cli) with support for additional AI\n6\tcoding agents.\n7\t\n8\tPlease read the [Entire CLI Code of Conduct](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n9\tbefore participating.\n10\t\n11\t> **New to Entire?** See the [First-Time Contributors guide](doc/first-time-contributors.md)\n12\t> for a step-by-step first contribution walkthrough, or the [README](README.md)\n13\t> for setup and architecture documentation.\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## Before You Code: Discuss First\n18\t\n19\tThe fastest way to get a contribution merged is to align with maintainers before\n20\twriting code. Please **open an issue first** describing what you want to change,\n21\tand wait for maintainer feedback before starting implementation. This is\n22\tespecially true for new external agents -- adding a new `entire-agent-<name>` is\n23\ta long-running commitment that the maintainers will need to support.\n24\t\n25\t### Contribution Workflow\n26\t\n27\t1. **Open an issue** describing the problem, feature, or new agent\n28\t2. **Wait for maintainer feedback**: we may have relevant context or plans\n29\t3. **Get approval** before starting implementation\n30\t4. **Submit your PR** referencing the approved issue\n31\t5. **Address all feedback** including automated Copilot comments\n32\t6. **Maintainer review and merge**\n33\t\n34\t---\n35\t\n36\t## First-Time Contributors\n37\t\n38\tNew to the project? Welcome! Start with the\n39\t[First-Time Contributors guide](doc/first-time-contributors.md). It explains\n40\thow to find a comfortable issue, ask for a scoped starter task, set up the\n41\trepo, use AI responsibly, run the right checks, and open your first pull\n42\trequest.\n43\t\n44\t### Starter Contributions\n45\t\n46\tWe recommend starting with:\n47\t\n48\t- **A protocol compliance gap**: An existing agent fails a check against\n49\t  [`entireio/external-agents-tests`](https://github.com/entireio/external-agents-tests)\n50\t  on your machine; add a focused fix.\n51\t- **A lifecycle test failure you can reproduce**: The `e2e/` harness flagged\n52\t  something; capture it as a narrower test and a fix.\n53\t- **Confusing output or help text** in an existing agent's CLI.\n54\t- **Documentation friction**: Improve this repo's README, agent READMEs, or\n55\t  contributor docs after you hit a real problem.\n56\t- **An agent unit test** that covers existing behavior without changing it.\n57\t\n58\tAdding a brand-new `entire-agent-<name>` is welcome but is not a first-PR\n59\tshape. Open an issue first and expect the work to span multiple PRs.\n60\t\n61\tBrowse [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/external-agents/issues), or\n62\task in the `#looking-for-contributors` channel on the\n63\t[Entire Discord](https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S) if you want help finding a\n64\tstarter-sized slice.\n65\t\n66\tUsing a coding agent while contributing is welcome -- this repo is literally\n67\tabout coding-agent integration -- but you are responsible for the final diff.\n68\tReview AI-generated changes yourself before opening a PR.\n69\t\n70\t---\n71\t\n72\t## Submitting Issues\n73\t\n74\tAll feature requests, bug reports, and general issues should be submitted\n75\tthrough [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/external-agents/issues).\n76\tPlease search for existing issues before opening a new one.\n77\t\n78\tFor security-related issues, see the Security section below.\n79\t\n80\t---\n81\t\n82\t## Security\n83\t\n84\tIf you discover a security vulnerability, **do not report it through GitHub\n85\tIssues**. Instead, follow the disclosure process described in the\n86\t[Entire CLI SECURITY.md](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/main/SECURITY.md).\n87\tAll security reports are kept confidential.\n88\t\n89\t---\n90\t\n91\t## Communication\n92\t\n93\tContributions and communications are expected to occur through:\n94\t\n95\t- [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/external-agents/issues): Bug\n96\t  reports and feature requests\n97\t- [Discord](https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S): Questions, general conversation,\n98\t  and real-time support\n99\t\n100\tPlease represent the project and community respectfully in all public and\n101\tprivate interactions.\n102\t\n103\t---\n104\t\n105\t## How to Contribute\n106\t\n107\tThere are many ways to contribute:\n108\t\n109\t- **Fix or extend an existing agent**: `entire-agent-kiro` or\n110\t  `entire-agent-pi` under [`agents/`](agents/)\n111\t- **Improve the lifecycle harness**: The shared `e2e/` tests that exercise\n112\t  every agent\n113\t- **Add a new external agent**: Discuss in an issue first; the\n114\t  [external agent builder skill](.claude/skills/entire-external-agent/) walks\n115\t  you through the full pipeline\n116\t- **Documentation**: Improve READMEs, agent docs, contributor instructions\n117\t- **Community**: Help others on Discord, answer questions, share knowledge\n118\t\n119\t---\n120\t\n121\t## Reporting Bugs\n122\t\n123\tGood bug reports help us fix issues quickly. When reporting a bug, please\n124\tinclude:\n125\t\n126\t### Required Information\n127\t\n128\t1. **Affected agent**: e.g. `entire-agent-kiro`, `entire-agent-pi`, or \"the\n129\t   `e2e/` harness\"\n130\t2. **Entire CLI version**: run `entire version`\n131\t3. **Operating system**\n132\t4. **Go version**: run `go version`\n133\t5. **mise version**: run `mise --version`\n134\t\n135\t### What to Include\n136\t\n137\t1. **What did you do?**: Include the exact commands you ran\n138\t2. **What did you expect to happen?**\n139\t3. **What actually happened?**: Include the full error message or unexpected\n140\t   output (especially the JSON returned by the agent if a protocol check\n141\t   failed)\n142\t4. **Can you reproduce it?**: Does it happen every time or intermittently?\n143\t5. **Any additional context?**: Logs, lifecycle artifacts from\n144\t   `e2e/artifacts/`, related issues\n145\t\n146\t---\n147\t\n148\t## Local Setup\n149\t\n150\t### Prerequisites\n151\t\n152\t- **Go 1.26.x**: mise will install the pinned version\n153\t- **mise**: Task runner and version manager. Install with\n154\t  `curl https://mise.run | sh`\n155\t- **The target agent's own CLI** if you plan to run lifecycle tests against it\n156\t  (e.g. `kiro`, `pi`). Each agent's README under [`agents/`](agents/) lists\n157\t  what it expects.\n158\t\n159\t### Clone and Install\n160\t\n161\t```bash\n162\t# Clone the repository\n163\tgit clone https://github.com/entireio/external-agents.git\n164\tcd external-agents\n165\t\n166\t# Trust the mise configuration (required on first setup)\n167\tmise trust\n168\t\n169\t# Install pinned tools (Go, golangci-lint, license_finder, ...)\n170\tmise install\n171\t\n172\t# Build every agent binary into ./bin\n173\tmise run build\n174\t\n175\t# Verify setup by running unit tests across all agents\n176\tmise run test\n177\t```\n178\t\n179\tSee the [README](README.md) for the wider repository layout and the testing\n180\tsplit between protocol compliance, lifecycle integration, and unit tests.\n181\t\n182\t---\n183\t\n184\t## Making Changes\n185\t\n186\t1. **Create a branch** for your changes:\n187\t\n188\t   ```bash\n189\t   git checkout -b fix/short-description\n190\t   ```\n191\t\n192\t2. **Make your changes**: follow the [Code Style](#code-style) guidelines\n193\t   and keep the change narrow.\n194\t\n195\t3. **Test your changes**: see [Testing](#testing).\n196\t\n197\t4. **Commit** with clear, descriptive messages:\n198\t\n199\t   ```bash\n200\t   git commit -m \"kiro: clarify missing-config error\"\n201\t   ```\n202\t\n203\t   When a commit touches a single agent, prefix the subject with the agent\n204\t   name (e.g. `kiro:`, `pi:`). Cross-cutting changes (the lifecycle harness,\n205\t   shared docs, CI) can omit the prefix.\n206\t\n207\t---\n208\t\n209\t## Code Style\n210\t\n211\tFollow standard Go idioms and conventions.\n212\t\n213\t### Key Points\n214\t\n215\t- **Error handling**: Handle all errors explicitly -- don't leave them\n216\t  unchecked.\n217\t- **Formatting**: Code must pass `gofmt` (run `mise run fmt`).\n218\t- **Linting**: Code must pass `golangci-lint`. The config lives at\n219\t  [.golangci.yaml](.golangci.yaml).\n220\t- **Naming**: Use meaningful, descriptive names following Go conventions.\n221\t- **Protocol surface**: When changing a subcommand's JSON output, keep it\n\n... [207 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d4f20a9c-b4cd-4584-a4d7-901e0994739d","timestamp":"2026-05-12T16:43:23.032Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/goose-guest/Documents/work/external-agents/.claude/worktrees/nervous-lovelace-2f4b1f","sessionId":"5ec529ca-57a1-47f3-a7d2-fb63984f64a9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"claude/nervous-lovelace-2f4b1f"}
